Gold is and always has been currency.  There is no better proof than the fact that every central bank in the world has large holdings of gold.
<br>
"According to the World Gold Council, central banks collectively bought 651.5 tonnes of gold in 2018, the most purchases in more than 50 years."  -  bit.ly/2K2lMDu  -  How much gold do central banks hold?  -  https://bit.ly/2uPGbBz
<br>
<br>
But gold is not as easy to manipulate as FIAT currency.  You cannot simply print more of it.  
<br>

In times of high volatility and crisis gold is considered a safe haven to protect purchasing power.
